.TH "ANIMATIONPLAYBACKEVENT.CURRENTTIME" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
AnimationPlaybackEvent.currentTime \- AnimationPlaybackEvent:
currentTime property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]currentTime\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]AnimationPlaybackEvent\f[R] interface represents the current time
of the animation that generated the event at the moment the event is
queued.
For browser\-generated \f[CR]cancel\f[R] events, the value is
\f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH VALUE
A number representing the current time in milliseconds, or
\f[CR]null\f[R].
.PP
When a value is supplied to the \f[CR]AnimationPlaybackEvent()\f[R]
constructor, Chrome and Firefox do not apply timer rounding to the
returned value.
In Safari, the browser rounds the returned value to 0.001 ms, the
resolution used to represent animation times.
.PP
For browser\-generated \f[CR]finish\f[R] and \f[CR]remove\f[R] events,
this property inherits the value and precision of
\f[CR]Animation.currentTime\f[R] when the event is queued, without
introducing additional inaccuracy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Web Animations API
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]AnimationPlayBackEvent\f[R]
